Article 5 The amount of compensation for mental damage shall be determined according to the following factors:
(1) the degree of fault of the infringer, unless otherwise provided by law;
(2) the specific circumstances such as the purpose, manner, and occasion of the infringing act;
(3) the consequences caused by the infringing act;
(4) the gains obtained by the infringer;
(5) the economic capacity of the infringer to bear liability;
(6) the average living standard of the place where the court accepting the case is located.
